{"version":"ai-mcq-bank-v2-la-batch15-high-quality-rewritten-affected-2026-05-22-stem-fixed-inequality-rendering-fixed-student-facing-qc-2026-05-31-pt-foundations-2026-06-11-pt-batch2-foundations-counting-2026-06-11-pt-batch3-counting-probability-rules-2026-06-11-pt-batch4-conditioning-2026-06-11-pt-batch5-random-variables-2026-06-11-pt-batch6-discrete-distributions-2026-06-11-pt-batch7-distribution-foundations-2026-06-11-pt-batch8-continuous-expectation-2026-06-11-pt-batch9-non-week7-expectation-transform-2026-06-11-pt-batch10-non-week7-process-summary-2026-06-11-pt-batch11-non-week7-final-summary-shape-2026-06-11-quality-round1-2026-06-14-quality-round2-2026-06-14-quality-round3-2026-06-14-quality-round4-deep-2026-06-14+quality-round5-difficulty-2026-06-14+quality-round6-expression-2026-06-14+quality-round7-answer-cue-2026-06-14+quality-round8-answer-shape-2026-06-14+quality-round9-answer-position-2026-06-14+quality-round10-template-padding-2026-06-14+quality-round11-generic-stems-2026-06-14+quality-round12-deterministic-cleanup-2026-06-15+quality-pilot-deep-rework-2026-06-15+v3-2026-10-04+upright-2026-10-04+v3-2026-10-04+v3-2026-10-06+v3-2026-10-06+qa-fixes-2026-10-08","concept_id":"Year-1/2b-Probability-Distributions/marginal-probability-density-function.html","concept":{"concept_id":"Year-1/2b-Probability-Distributions/marginal-probability-density-function.html","questions":[{"id":"year_1_2b_probability_distributions_marginal_probability_density_function_91487ddf_001","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"conceptual","question":"For a jointly continuous pair with density $f_{X,Y}$, how is the marginal density of $X$ obtained?","options":["$f_X(x)=\\int f_{X,Y}(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}x$","$f_X(x)=f_{X,Y}(x,x)$","$f_X(x)=\\int f_{X,Y}(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}y$","$f_X(x)=\\max_yf_{X,Y}(x,y)$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"7345defbe62e0d1c20907077","time_limit":20},{"id":"year_1_2b_probability_distributions_marginal_probability_density_function_91487ddf_002","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"conceptual","question":"A joint density is strictly positive on $0<x<y<1$ and zero elsewhere. For fixed $0<x<1$, which set contains exactly the $y$ values where the joint density is positive?","options":["$0<y<1$","$x<y<1$","$0<y<x$","$0<y<1-x$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"b47ba4acb2926f6c4ae26a63","time_limit":25},{"id":"year_1_2b_probability_distributions_marginal_probability_density_function_91487ddf_003","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Why does every marginal density integrate to $1$?","options":["Integrating $f_X$ integrates $f_{X,Y}$ over the plane","A marginal density never takes values above $1$","$X$ and $Y$ are assumed to be independent","Each slice $y\\mapsto f_{X,Y}(x,y)$ integrates to $1$ by itself"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"056d8a28cc158a4bfae7995d","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_1_2b_probability_distributions_marginal_probability_density_function_91487ddf_004","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"conceptual","question":"What is $f_X(x)$ at an $x$ for which the vertical line through $x$ misses the support of $f_{X,Y}$?","options":["$1$","Undefined","The value of $f_Y$ at $x$","$0$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"23e4e68e398ad2d38c8803a7","time_limit":25},{"id":"year_1_2b_probability_distributions_marginal_probability_density_function_91487ddf_005","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Suppose $f_{X,Y}(x,y)=g(x)h(y)$ for all $x,y$, where $g$ and $h$ are densities. What is $f_X$?","options":["$g(x)\\,h(x)$","$g$","$h$","$g(x)+h(x)$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"8508fc58e8d4ee6d9e24219d","time_limit":25},{"id":"year_1_2b_probability_distributions_marginal_probability_density_function_91487ddf_006","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"The pair $(X,Y)$ has joint density $3y$ on the triangle $0<x<y<1$ and zero elsewhere. Find the marginal density of $X$ on $(0,1)$.","options":["$\\tfrac32(1-x^2)$","$3x^2$","$\\tfrac32$","$\\tfrac32x^2$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"63848d64da977a7f92cd35fd","time_limit":25},{"id":"year_1_2b_probability_distributions_marginal_probability_density_function_91487ddf_007","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"$(X,Y)$ is uniform on the unit disc $x^2+y^2<1$. What is $f_X(x)$ for $-1<x<1$?","options":["$\\tfrac1\\pi$","$\\sqrt{1-x^2}$","$2\\sqrt{1-x^2}$","$\\tfrac2\\pi\\sqrt{1-x^2}$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"d82b4ec0430cc8d064e43f99","time_limit":25},{"id":"year_1_2b_probability_distributions_marginal_probability_density_function_91487ddf_008","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"The pair $(X,Y)$ has density $x+y$ on $0<x<1$, $0<y<1$, and zero elsewhere. Which marginal density does $Y$ have on $(0,1)$?","options":["$2y$","$y+\\tfrac12$","$y$","$1$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"227b7f7ba99e8f1d1f8fd72a","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_1_2b_probability_distributions_marginal_probability_density_function_91487ddf_009","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"With joint density $2\\mathrm{e}^{-x-y}$ on $0<x<y$ and zero elsewhere, which density does $X$ have on $(0,\\infty)$?","options":["$\\mathrm{e}^{-x}$","$2\\mathrm{e}^{-2x}$","$2\\mathrm{e}^{-x}$","$2\\mathrm{e}^{-x}(1-\\mathrm{e}^{-x})$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"118bd64429c4a5b3d8e4b590","time_limit":25},{"id":"year_1_2b_probability_distributions_marginal_probability_density_function_91487ddf_010","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"The joint density of $(X,Y)$ is $\\tfrac1{35}$ on $0<x<7$, $0<y<5$, and zero elsewhere. Using the marginal density of $X$, find $\\mathbb{P}(2<X<6)$.","options":["$\\tfrac4{35}$","$\\tfrac67$","$\\tfrac27$","$\\tfrac47$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"6b56e36e78970dd73fc2d533","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_1_2b_probability_distributions_marginal_probability_density_function_91487ddf_011","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Let $(X,Y)$ have joint density $f_{X,Y}$ and define $m(x)=\\int_{\\mathbb{R}}f_{X,Y}(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}y$. Which identity explains why $m$ is a marginal density of $X$, for every $a<b$?","options":["$\\mathbb{P}(a<X<b)=m(a)$","$\\mathbb{P}(a<X<b)=\\int_a^b m(x)\\,\\mathrm{d}x$","$\\mathbb{P}(a<X<b)=\\dfrac1{b-a}\\int_a^b m(x)\\,\\mathrm{d}x$","$\\mathbb{P}(a<X<b)=\\int_a^b f_{X,Y}(x,x)\\,\\mathrm{d}x$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"6ada152242ca67d565e1aa60","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_1_2b_probability_distributions_marginal_probability_density_function_91487ddf_012","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"$(X,Y)$ is uniform on a triangle of positive area. What determines how $f_X(x)$ varies with $x$?","options":["Nothing: $X$ is uniform as well","The density of $Y$ at $x$","The length of the vertical slice at $x$","The area of the triangle only"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"615d4127e2db7bbb4151cb40","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_1_2b_probability_distributions_marginal_probability_density_function_91487ddf_013","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Let $(X,Y)$ have joint density $f_{X,Y}$ and satisfy $\\mathbb{E}[|X|]<\\infty$. Which formula always gives $\\mathbb{E}[X]$?","options":["$\\iint_{\\mathbb{R}^2}x\\,f_{X,Y}(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\,\\mathrm{d}y$","$\\iint_{\\mathbb{R}^2}xy\\,f_{X,Y}(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\,\\mathrm{d}y$","$\\int_{\\mathbb{R}}x\\,f_{X,Y}(x,x)\\,\\mathrm{d}x$","$\\int_{\\mathbb{R}}x\\,f_Y(x)\\,\\mathrm{d}x$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"de91953732ac05dc0ae524b4","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_1_2b_probability_distributions_marginal_probability_density_function_91487ddf_014","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"For the joint density $6(x-y)$ on $0<y<x<1$ and zero elsewhere, compute the marginal density of $Y$ on $(0,1)$.","options":["$3y^2$","$6(1-y)^2$","$3(1-y)$","$3(1-y)^2$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"72e8d451fdbfedbcb54fb215","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_1_2b_probability_distributions_marginal_probability_density_function_91487ddf_015","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"Let $(X,Y)$ have density $\\tfrac12\\mathrm{e}^{-y}$ on $|x|<y$ and zero elsewhere. What is $f_X(x)$?","options":["$\\tfrac12\\mathrm{e}^{-|x|}$","$\\mathrm{e}^{-|x|}$","$\\tfrac12\\mathrm{e}^{-x}$ for $x>0$, and $0$ otherwise","$|x|\\mathrm{e}^{-|x|}$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"d7aa5c3fdfa81bda7b927535","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_1_2b_probability_distributions_marginal_probability_density_function_91487ddf_016","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"$(X,Y)$ is uniform on the region $0<x<1$, $0<y<x^2$. What is $f_X(x)$ for $0<x<1$?","options":["$x^2$","$1$","$3x^2$","$3x$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"3802999341e00aae7f246b7c","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_1_2b_probability_distributions_marginal_probability_density_function_91487ddf_017","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Each expression below defines a joint density on $0<x<1$, $0<y<1$, with value zero elsewhere. Which has both marginals uniform on $(0,1)$ without being constant?","options":["$1+\\tfrac12(2x-1)y$","$1+\\tfrac12x(2y-1)$","$1+\\tfrac12(2x-1)(2y-1)$","$1+\\tfrac12(2x-1)(2y-1)^2$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"8cedc0b3fd769bb9c82cba29","time_limit":40},{"id":"year_1_2b_probability_distributions_marginal_probability_density_function_91487ddf_018","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Let $(X,Y)$ have joint density $f_{X,Y}$ with marginal densities $f_X,f_Y$, fix $x$ with $0<f_X(x)<\\infty$, and let $f_{Y\\mid X}(\\cdot\\mid x)$ be the conditional density of $Y$ given $X=x$. In general, what is the area of the slice $y\\mapsto f_{X,Y}(x,y)$, and how is it related to $f_{Y\\mid X}(\\cdot\\mid x)$?","options":["Area $1$; the slice is the conditional density itself","Area $f_Y(x)$; the slice is the conditional density times $f_Y(x)$","Area $1$; the conditional density is the slice multiplied by $f_X(x)$","Area $f_X(x)$; the conditional density is the slice divided by $f_X(x)$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"54c873d4dbc63379bebbcbd5","time_limit":50},{"id":"year_1_2b_probability_distributions_marginal_probability_density_function_91487ddf_019","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"application","question":"$(X,Y)$ is uniform on the parallelogram $0<y<1$, $y<x<y+2$. Which is its marginal density $f_X(x)$? Values at the interval endpoints may be ignored.","options":["$f_X(x)=\\begin{cases}x/2,&0<x<1,\\\\1/2,&1<x<2,\\\\(3-x)/2,&2<x<3,\\\\0,&\\text{otherwise}.\\end{cases}$","$f_X(x)=\\begin{cases}x,&0<x<1,\\\\1,&1<x<2,\\\\3-x,&2<x<3,\\\\0,&\\text{otherwise}.\\end{cases}$","$f_X(x)=\\begin{cases}x/2,&0<x<1,\\\\1/2,&1<x<2,\\\\(x-2)/2,&2<x<3,\\\\0,&\\text{otherwise}.\\end{cases}$","$f_X(x)=\\begin{cases}1/3,&0<x<3,\\\\0,&\\text{otherwise}.\\end{cases}$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"c70e5cbd7dcb744b3553fa07","time_limit":40},{"id":"year_1_2b_probability_distributions_marginal_probability_density_function_91487ddf_020","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"application","question":"$(X,Y)$ is uniform on the region between $y=x^2$ and $y=x$ for $0<x<1$. What is $f_Y(y)$ for $0<y<1$?","options":["$6(y-y^2)$","$6(1-y)$","$6(\\sqrt y-y)$","$\\sqrt y-y$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"f7cbc443c20afcda5d57225b","time_limit":40}]}}